### ============================================================
### Workshop Management System — Manual Scenario Tests
### ============================================================
### Tool:  VS Code REST Client / JetBrains HTTP Client
### Docs:  https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=humao.rest-client
###
### Run order: Execute the requests TOP → BOTTOM.
### After Step 1 succeeds, copy the returned `requestId` from
### the response body and paste it into the @serviceRequestId
### variable below before executing Step 2.
### ============================================================

@baseUrl        = http://localhost:5085
@contentType    = application/json

# ── Seed IDs (replace with real GUIDs from your database) ────────────────────
@customerId     = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@mechanicId     = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
@vehicleId      = 33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333

# ── Captured from Step 1 response — fill in before running Step 2 ─────────────
@serviceRequestId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000


### ============================================================
### SCENARIO 1: Customer Check-In & Service Request Creation
### Business Flow:
###   A customer drives in with a vehicle for repair work.
###   The receptionist logs the request, assigns an available
###   mechanic, and records the agreed service price.
###   The factory pattern will detect RequestType = Repair and
###   instantiate a RepairRequest entity automatically.
### ============================================================

### [STEP 1] POST — Create a new Repair Service Request
# Expected: 201 Created
# Response body will contain the new ServiceRequest's `requestId`.
# Copy that value into @serviceRequestId above before running Step 2.

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/reception/create
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "requestType": 0,
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "mechanicId": "{{mechanicId}}",
  "vehicleId": "{{vehicleId}}",
  "price": 350.00,
  "commissionType": 1,
  "commissionValue": 10,
  "description": "Customer reports engine knocking noise and difficulty starting. Full engine diagnostic and repair requested."
}

###


### ============================================================
### SCENARIO 2: Inspection & Quotation Generation
### Business Flow:
###   After the mechanic inspects the vehicle, they identify the
###   required parts and labour. A formal quotation is generated
###   and attached to the existing ServiceRequest. The request
###   status transitions automatically to PendingCustomerApproval.
###
### ⚠ Pre-condition: @serviceRequestId must be set (from Step 1).
### ============================================================

### [STEP 2] POST — Generate a Quotation for the Service Request
# Expected: 201 Created
# Response body will contain the new Quotation's `quotationId` and `grandTotal`.

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/requests/{{serviceRequestId}}/quotations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "items": [
    {
      "type": 0,
      "description": "Engine Air Filter (OEM)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "unitPrice": 45.00
    },
    {
      "type": 0,
      "description": "Spark Plugs — Set of 4 (NGK Iridium)",
      "quantity": 4,
      "unitPrice": 18.50
    },
    {
      "type": 0,
      "description": "Engine Oil — 5W-30 Synthetic (5L)",
      "quantity": 2,
      "unitPrice": 38.00
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "description": "Full Engine Diagnostic & Compression Test",
      "quantity": 1,
      "unitPrice": 80.00
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "description": "Spark Plugs Replacement Labour",
      "quantity": 2,
      "unitPrice": 30.00
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Engine knock caused by worn spark plugs and dirty air filter. Oil change also recommended. All parts are OEM or equivalent grade. Estimated completion: 3 working hours."
}

###
